## 9. PRESERVE AND STRENGTHEN FIFO QUEUE FUNCTIONALITY

The existing application may contain queue-management concepts and FIFO logic.

Preserve existing queue and booking functionality.

If FIFO is already implemented, inspect it and fix any bugs without replacing the entire system.

FIFO means First In, First Out: the first eligible item entering a queue is processed before later eligible items.

Requirements:

* Maintain a reliable queue order.
* Preserve the original queue sequence when appropriate.
* Store queue records persistently in the existing database.
* Avoid duplicate queue entries caused by repeated submissions.
* Prevent simultaneous requests from corrupting queue state.
* Keep queue updates consistent between devices.
* Reflect booking or queue status correctly in the user interface.
* Preserve any existing business rules for urgency or priority.

IMPORTANT: FIFO and urgency-based prioritization are not identical.

If the application already has an emergency or priority mechanism, preserve its intended rules. Do not silently replace an existing priority queue with strict FIFO.

Do not add FIFO demonstrations, queue diagrams, data-structure explanations, or unnecessary educational panels to the login screen.

Keep technical queue logic in the relevant application components and backend services.

